@why APM: the defect register (TN-apm-defect-register.md, 2026-08-27) defined the right standard — "guaranteed" means the defect cannot recur without a named mechanism failing — recorded 24 of 26 defects at "guarantee: none", and then sat as evidence rather than a work queue; twelve days later the singleton parks it predicted duly arrived. The end-to-end causal analysis (790c0491) happened within HOURS of the first deliberately scheduled halt, after weeks of patching a live campaign.
@how own mechanism: halts are scheduled at wave boundaries; the defect register is the work queue for the halt; no new wave starts until the top "guarantee: none" rows have mechanisms.
@violation-signature Register rows marked "guarantee: none" age across wave boundaries untouched; seam-level rebuilds happen only after an operator-forced halt; every fixing session runs against a live campaign.
! conclusion: Halt-and-consolidate is scheduled at wave boundaries, with the defect register as its work queue — no new wave until the top "guarantee: none" rows have mechanisms — because seam rebuilds never fit inside sessions patching a live system.

  + context: A campaign runs in waves; defects arrive continuously; every agent session that touches the apparatus does so while the campaign is mid-flight and data is accumulating.

  + IF:
    Fixes keep landing but the same defect families keep recurring.

  + HOWEVER:
    Against a live campaign, every fix is minimal by necessity — nobody is ever authorized or situated to stop and rebuild a seam, because stopping always costs something visible today while the seam's cost is spread across future incidents.

  + THEN:
    Put the halt on the schedule so it needs no one's courage: between waves, stop cleanly, re-read the register, and convert "guarantee: none" rows into mechanisms — the register defines done as "recurrence requires a named mechanism to fail". Only then start the next wave. Register stewards drain between waves so no raw queue reaches the operator.

  + BECAUSE:
    Analysis capacity exists — the register's standard and the causal through-line were both produced by the same agents who spent weeks patching — but it activates only when the system is stopped; unscheduled, that happens exactly when the operator's patience breaks, which is the most expensive possible trigger.

    + evidence: APM: 08-27 register standard unused for twelve days; 09-08 end-to-end analysis within hours of the forced halt. Convergent wm mechanism: self-halting loop that bells its owner; ruled walkthroughs as scheduled halts; steward drain contract.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - Define your wave boundary and put the halt in the coordinator, not in the operator's judgment.
    - Make "top N register rows have mechanisms" the precondition the next wave's start checks mechanically.
